unidoc_construction_0175,5,page-12-chunk-1,12,0.5674660205841064,0.13028541207313538,"MINUTES, LIMESTONE COUNTY COMMISSION, MAY 3, 2021 COMMISSION MEETING 12 an awesome job, would be graduating at that graduat ion. Chairman Daly also complimented the Veteran’s Museum and thanked everyone for coming to the meeting. Adjourned at 10:27. a.m. until 9:00 a.m. on Tuesday, May 17, 2021, at the Clinton Street Courthouse Annex, 100 South Clinton Street, Athens, Alabama.",379
unidoc_construction_0175,6,page-1-chunk-1,1,0.5951396226882935,0.12168575078248978,"MINUTES, LIMESTONE COUNTY COMMISSION, MAY 3, 2021 COMMISSION MEETING 1 The Limestone County Commission met in a regular meeting today, at 10:00 a.m. at the Clinton Street Courthouse Annex, 100 South Clinton Street, Athens, Alabama. Present: Daryl Sammet, Danny Barksdale, Jason Black, and LaDon Townsend. Absent: None. Collin Daly, Chairman presided. Gary Chaynoweth addressed the Commission and stated, “I’m actually a City of Madison resident, and I have been the City Engineer for the past 16 years. I’m going to be retiring soon, and before I retired, I wanted to come here and thank the Limestone County Commission. During the last eight or nine years, we have had several joint projects where we have shared resources to get some road work done, and it has made my life much easier, and it’s been very good for both of our residents. I just wanted to come here and say thank you very much.” Teresa Todd, President of Athens-Limestone County Tourism Association, requested to use the steps of the Courthouse for “Singing on the Square. She also requested assistance with the “Rural Conference” as far as meals, tours and transportation. Lastly, she mentioned the Sheriff’s Rodeo happening during the week of May 8th, and she noted that the rodeo is one of tourism’s best times. The meeting began with the Pledge of Allegiance. MOTION was made by Danny Barksdale and seconded by Jason Black to approve the minutes of April 19, 2021. The Chairman asked if there was any discussion. There was no discussion. The Administrator called the roll. Danny Barksdale, aye; Jason Black, aye; Daryl Sammet, aye; and LaDon Townsend, aye. Motion carries unanimously. MOTION was made by Daryl Sammet and seconded by Danny Barksdale to approve the following claims: 4/16/2021 Check # 61185 - 61252 $ 548,471.72 4/23/2021 Check # 61253 - 61310 $ 769,768.06 4/29/2021 Check # 61311 $ 144.25 TOTAL $1,318,384.03 with detailed claims of the above being on file for review upon request to the County Administrator. The Chairman asked if there was any discussion. There was no discussion. The Administrator called the roll. Daryl Sammet, aye; Danny Barksdale, aye; Jason Black, aye; and LaDon Townsend, aye. Motion carries unanimously.",2217
unidoc_construction_0175,7,page-2-chunk-1,2,0.4731718599796295,0.09534946829080582,"MINUTES, LIMESTONE COUNTY COMMISSION, MAY 3, 2021 COMMISSION MEETING 2 MOTION was made by Danny Barksdale to approve a Resolution to prohibit through truck traffic on Bradford Road and the north section of Newby Road, from Gray Road to Highway 72, and providing placement of both “No Thru Trucks” and “Local Deliveries Only” signs at said location(s). Motion failed for lack of second. MOTION was made by Jason Black and seconded by Daryl Sammet to approve a Consultation Services Agreement between Martin & Cobey Construction Company and the Limestone County Commission. CONSULTATION SERVICES AGREEMENT Between MARTIN & COBEY CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INC. And THE LIMESTONE COUNTY corvnnss10N THIS CONSULTATION SERVICES AGREEMENT (hereinafter ""Agreement"") is entered into on this this day of by and between MARTIN & COBEY CONSTRUC TION COMPANY, and THE LIMESONTE COUNTY COMMISSION, Athens, Alabama(""Owner""). In consideration of the mutual promises set forth below and other good and valuable consideration, the receipt of which is hereby acknowledged, the Owner and Consultant agree as follows: ARTICLE 1 CONSULTANT'S RESPONSIBILITIES 1.2 The Consultant's services consist of those services performed by the Consultant, Consultant's agents, and Consultant's employees as enumerated in Article 2 of this Agreement. 1.3 The Consultant shall provide sufficient organization, personnel, and management to carry out the requirements of this Agreement in an expeditious and economical manner consistent with the interests of the Owner. ARTICLE 2 SCOPE OF CONSULTANT'S SERVICES BASIC SERVICES 2.1 The Consultant shall perform a detailed cost analysis and constructability for various new construction projects, renovation projects, demolition projects, roofing projects and preconstruction services for the Owner at such times as requested by the Owner. 2.2 The Consultant shall assist the Owner with bidding and subcontracting on various projects listed in article 2.1 as well as over see work crews provided by the Owner for various and miscellaneous maintenance projects as listed in article 2.1.",2090
