unidoc_construction_0199,27,page-21-chunk-1,21,0.4786997437477112,0.000191104321856983,"21 should be completed in a reasonable amount of time, not to exceed 30 days. If you have any questions regarding your warranty rights and responsibilities, you should contact your nearest authorized service center, call Poulan at 1- -800- -554- -6723, or send e-mail corre- spondence to emission.warranty@HCOP- - emission.com. WARRANTY COMMENCE- MENT DATE: The warranty period begins on the date the small off- -road engine is pur- chased. LENGTH OF COVERAGE: This warranty shall be for a period of two years from the initial date of purchase. WHAT IS COVERED: REPAIR OR REPLACEMENT OF PARTS. Repair or replacement of any warranted part will be performed at no charge to the owner at an approved Poulan servicing center. If you have any questions regarding your warranty rights and responsi- bilities, you should contact your nearest au- thorized service center, call Poulan at 1- -800- -554- -6723, or send e-mail corre- spondence to emission.warranty@ HCOP- - emission.com. WARRANTY PERIOD: Any warranted part which is not scheduled for re- placement as required maintenance, or which is scheduled only for regular inspec- tion to the effect of “repair or replace as nec- essary” shall be warranted for 2 years. Any warranted part which is scheduled for re- placement as required maintenance shall be warranted for the period of time up to the first scheduled replacement point for that part. DIAGNOSIS: The owner shall not be charged for diagnostic labor which leads to the determination that a warranted part is de- fective if the diagnostic work is performed at an approved Poulan servicing center. CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES: Poulan may be liable for damages to other engine components caused by the failure of a war- ranted part still under warranty. WHAT IS NOT COVERED : All failures caused by abuse, neglect, or improper maintenance are not covered. ADD- -ON OR MODIFIED PARTS:The use of add- -on or modified parts can be grounds for disallowing a warranty claim. Poulan is not liable to cover failures of warranted parts caused by the use of add- - on or modified parts. HOW TO FILE A CLAIM: If you have any questions regarding your warranty rights and responsibilities, you should contact your nearest authorized service center, call Poulan at 1- -800- -554- -6723, or send e-mail corre- spondence to emission.warranty@HCOP- - emission.com. WHERE TO GET WARRAN- TY SERVICE: Warranty services or repairs shall be provided at all Poulan service centers. Call: 1- -800- -554- -6723 or send e-mail corre- spondence to emission.warranty@ HCOP -- emission.com. MAINTENANCE, REPLACE- MENT AND REPAIR OF EMISSION RELATED PARTS : Any Poulan approved replacement part used in the performance of any warranty maintenance or repair on emis- sion related parts will be provided without charge to the owner if the part is under war- ranty. EMISSION CONTROL WARRANTY PARTS LIST:Carburetor, air filter (covered up to maintenance schedule), ignition system: spark plug (covered up to maintenance sched- ule), ignition module, muffler including catalyst (if equipped), fuel tank. MAINTENANCE STATEMENT :The owner is responsible for the performance of all required maintenance as defined in the instruction manual. The information on the product label indicates which standard your engine is certified. Example: (Year) EPA and/or CALIFORNIA. This engine is certified to be emissions compliant for the following use: Moderate (50 hours) Intermediate (125 hours) Extended (300 hours)",3470
unidoc_crm_0001,1,page-1-chunk-1,1,0.45832177996635437,0.6460136771202087,"1 | Page The Bowmanville Older Adult Association Board of Directors, Staff and Reopening Task Force will be working towards reopening, offering small in person outdoor activities, drive thru events while also keeping our virtual programs, events and activities available on Zoom and over the phone. Updates should always be expected – based on public health directives, dates and times are subject to change without notice. We will continue to monitor the situation, doing our best to make the right decisions for our members, our team and our community. What is important for all to remember is that this will only be possible if we are able to meet all Federal, Provincial, Regional & Municipal guidelines. Our organization continues to be committed to continuing to provide safe and exceptional older adult programming, services and events to our members. Effective immediately our Front Desk, Office, Outdoor tent and some larger indoor spaces along with our Footcare area will reopen Monday to Friday 9 am to 4 pm. Strict capacity limits will be in place and all members and guests will be required to prescreen (includes a temperature check and waiver completion) prior to admission and participation. We encourage BOAA members to access our FREE virtual activities via: ☑ ZOOM ☑ Phone Programming ☑ Care Calls ☑ Books & Puzzles Pick-Up and Delivery ☑ Videos Available on BOAA’s YouTube https://www.youtube.com/c/BOAA2856/videos We truly appreciate the support you have offered us during these troubling times and we ask that you continue to make informed decisions while making sure you are always looking out for your health and safety. Reach out to us if you have questions or require further information. We will get through this together. #BOAAStrong Emergency Contact: Angie at ☎ 905-242-5585 or 📩📩 execdirector@bowmanvilleolderadults.com",1850
unidoc_crm_0001,2,page-5-chunk-1,5,0.4687957465648651,0.07159119844436646,"5 | Page NEW BINGO WITH TEAM BOAA Under the “B” … under the “I” … under the “N” … you get the idea. Bring your own dabber and we will provide the disposable cards. $3 per person for as many cards as you wish to play with small cash prizes to be won. Tuesday 1 pm to 2:15 pm Running weekly until August 31st *Due to tennis court resurfacing programs scheduled after August 23rd may have to be cancelled please watch for future updates NEW BOAA CHOIR with Allanah Coles & Donna Barber Join together to sing a few songs and enjoy the fellowship of others. Wednesday 9:30 am to 10:30 am Running weekly until August 25th *Due to tennis court resurfacing programs scheduled after August 23rd may have to be cancelled please watch for future updates $2 per member drop-in fee applies for all participants NEW SOCIAL ART Join our artistic members who have a common hobby to chat, share ideas, and show each other your progress on projects. Wednesday 11 am to 12:30 pm Running weekly until August 25th *Due to tennis court resurfacing programs scheduled after August 23rd may have to be cancelled please watch for future updates $2 per member drop-in fee applies for all participants NEW HORSESHOES Fun, social afternoon with friends tossing horseshoes while enjoying the sunshine and great outdoors. Each week teams will be created by random draw. All equipment provided but feel free to bring your own if you like. Wednesday 1:30 pm to 3 pm Running weekly until August 18th $2 per member drop-in fee applies for all participants NEW TABLE TENNIS Have fun and exercise playing a non-competitive game of table tennis. Singles play only unless partners reside in the same household. Tables are located in the main auditorium. Thursday 10 am to 12 pm Running weekly until August 26th $2 per member drop-in fee applies for all participants",1827
unidoc_crm_0001,3,page-6-chunk-1,6,0.3560856282711029,0.020332353189587593,"6 | Page NEW UKULELE DROP-IN If you play ukulele and know the basic chords, you will enjoy being a part of this group. Thursday 1 pm to 2:30 pm Running weekly until August 26th *Due to tennis court resurfacing programs scheduled after August 23rd may have to be cancelled please watch for future updates $2 per member drop-in fee applies for all participants SMALL IN-PERSON CONCERT SERIES NEW Alexa Goldie in CONCERT Singer/Songwriter Alexa Goldie has been singing since the age of 5. Alexa began writing music and performing in her hometown if Kingston when she was 12. At the age of 13, Alexa was discovered, signed, and shortly after flown down to Los Angeles to begin her musical journey. At the age of 22, Alexa has accomplished a lot; modelling for Turquoise, performing at the Listening Room Cafe in Nashville, Mayors Gala twice, T.I.F.F, the ACC (Air Canada Centre) for Rotary International and Beverly Hills Grammys Pre Party. Most recently, Alexa has released her debut country EP ‘High Road’ and been awarded with the ‘Rising Star’ and ‘Excellence in Songwriting’ awards by SongStudio. Thursday August 19th 12 pm $5 per member Limited seating. Pre-registration in advance required. Please contact the Team at BOAA to order yours today! NEW “SUNSHINE SERENADE” with Smile Theatre Rain or shine, the Smile Serenaders are bringing the sunshine to you this summer! Join us outside at Memorial Park in Bowmanville - for a 45 minute socially distanced performance, full of fun songs, interaction, and maybe even a dance move or two! Wednesday August 25th Pick the 1 pm or 2:30 pm SHOW! LOCATION UPDATE: MEMORIAL PARK – Liberty St. $5 per member Limited seating. Pre-registration in advance required. Please contact the Team at BOAA to order yours today!",1759
unidoc_crm_0001,4,page-10-chunk-1,10,0.45911478996276855,0.014503579586744308,"10 | Page SOCIAL ZOOM PARTY with Members of Team BOAA ALL BOAA Members are welcome to join us for our Social Zoom Party. Different topics or themes each week! Wednesday at 3 pm to 4:30 pm Running Weekly Until August 11th Click to join: https://bowmanvilleolderadults.zoom.us/j/98733700986?pwd=dzRQQ0wyam5NyjVGV09 POFBRZXRsUT09 Meeting ID: 987 3370 0986 Passcode: 149081 TOUR THE WORLD SCAVENGER HUNT Are you interested in touring around some of the most exciting cities in the world from the comfort of your home? Visit cities from all around the world. Every Friday you will be given a link with a different city and scavenger hunt list – simply click on the link, sit back in your chair and enjoy the tour on your screen while you take in the sights and catch answers to the questions. All without spending a penny on gas! You will have 7 days to fill out the scavenger hunt list for the specific city we will visit, and we invite you to join us on Zoom at the end of the following week to take up the answers with our Tour the World Scavenger Hunt team. Email events@bowmanvilleolderadults.com for your answers to be entered to win great prizes! Friday at 12 pm to 1 pm Running Weekly Until August 27th Pre-registration required. Please contact events@bowmanvilleolderadults.com to receive the Weekly Scavenger Hunt Questions & Zoom link. WHO KNEW? TRIVIA with Kristin, Sharon & Lauren Join us for an hour of fun and interactive trivia - different themes each week! Find out how much you know (or don't know) about everything under the sun. Please bring a pen and paper to track answers and scoring. Friday 1:30 pm to 2:30 pm August 20th - General Knowledge August 27th - Sports Click to join: https://bowmanvilleolderadults.zoom.us/j/93807109849?pwd=cGJHYlR0aU5SMzlvT0FoZ ktHQWhiQT09 Meeting ID: 938 0710 9849 Passcode: 300175",1830
unidoc_crm_0001,5,page-3-chunk-1,3,0.43030351400375366,0.012821214273571968,3 | Page SMALL IN-PERSON INDOOR/OUTDOOR GROUP ACTIVITIES • ALL IN-PERSON ACTIVITIES ARE CAPPED IN ORDER FOR US TO ADHERE TO THE UPDATED PROVINCIAL GUIDELINES FOR CAPACITY LIMITS • PRE-REGISTRATION IS REQUESTED TO AVOID DISAPPOINTMENT CAUSED BY CAPACITY LIMITS • PRESCREENING WITH TEMPERATURE CHECK REQUIRED PRIOR TO PARTICIPATION • NO SHARED EQUIPMENT • MASKS MUST BE WORN WHEN NOT SEATED OR WHEN PHYSICAL DISTANCING CANNOT BE MAINTAINED NEW SNOOKER Regulation snooker table provides for an excellent opportunity to enjoy a friendly match. Contact the front desk to pre-book a spot. Limit of two players per time slot and max of one time slot booking per person per day. Monday to Friday Choose either 9 am to 11 am or 1 pm to 3 pm $2 per member drop-in fee applies for all participants BOOK CLUB with Allanah Coles Meetings will be held once a month with options for both in-person. and virtual attendance. We will have an engaging discussion about the monthly book. Contact the BOAA for an updated book listing for upcoming titles and authors. If required a virtual attendance option can be made available. Contact Angie for details. Monday 10 am to 11:30 am August 16th $2 per member drop-in fee applies for all participants,1227
unidoc_crm_0001,6,page-18-chunk-1,18,0.31482386589050293,0.0034834241960197687,"18 | Page ZUMBA® STANDING OR SEATED with Veronica Vargas Using our split screen video technology, you will have the opportunity to choose the Zumba ® intensity you desire. The standing program will tone and sculpt your body while burning fat in an interval training mode. While the seated option will provide range of motion, low impact cardio and respiratory endurance. You will even have the opportunity to work your upper body only or kick it up a notch and use your lower body too. Tuesday NEW TIME 10:15 am to 11:15 am Running Weekly Until August 31st And Thursday NEW TIME 10:15 am to 11:15 am Running Weekly Until August 26th Click to join: https://zoom.us/j/99183869168?pwd=MUltRFpXakx4dEJyT0xrY3RjRUJjZz09 Meeting ID: 991 8386 9168 Password: 148328 ZUMBA® GOLD with Veronica Vargas A combination of dance and fitness created from the original Zumba ®. For the active older adult or beginner level participants who may need modifications for success. Monday NEW TIME 11:15 am to 12:15 pm Running Weekly Until August 30th No class August 2nd And Wednesday 10 am to 11 am Running Weekly Until August 25th Click to join: https://zoom.us/j/99183869168?pwd=MUltRFpXakx4dEJyT0xrY3RjRUJjZz09 Meeting ID: 991 8386 9168 Password: 148328 https://www.youtube.com/c/BOAA2856",1270
unidoc_crm_0001,7,page-12-chunk-1,12,0.3071860373020172,0.0017007224960252643,"12 | Page VIRTUAL GENERAL INTEREST PROGRAMS ON ZOOM: ASK A GENEALOGIST with Nancy Trimble, PLCGS Have you dabbled in your family history, but lost your way? Confused by all the expensive websites, and want to know if they are worth it? Have a question you need advice on? Then, come to our “Ask a Genealogist” drop-in hour and Nancy Trimble, chair of Durham Region Branch of Ontario Ancestors will help you. She has 50 years of experience in the genealogical field, with noted expertise in British and Ontario DNA research. The format will be very interactive with plenty of time to ask questions and discuss problems. Monday 1 pm to 1:55 pm Running Weekly Until August 16th No class August 2nd Click to join: https://bowmanvilleolderadults.zoom.us/j/99670095842?pwd=OUdUQ2VzRG9GK3ZNMn cxbUF5YWsxUT09 Meeting ID: 996 7009 5842 Passcode: 098778 CROCHETING with Doreen Cripps Join this social time with Doreen to receive information about crochet hooks, reading patterns, tips and tricks, stitches, stitch combinations, terminology, sources of information on the internet and videos. All levels of experience are welcome. Wednesday 2:30 pm to 3:45 pm Running Weekly Until August 25th Click to join: https://zoom.us/j/91409886110?pwd=a3JQTkU1YUpScXYrLzhmYjg0MWdmZz09 Meeting ID: 914 0988 6110 Password: 065308 NEW EN FRANÇAIS DROP-IN Join the meeting to keep in touch with the French-speaking members of BOAA. Tuesday 2:30 pm to 3:30 pm Running Weekly Until August 31st Click to join: https://zoom.us/j/97005924210?pwd=SkFES1lodTlWR3JTSnJ5VmVhbnJRUT09 Meeting ID: 970 0592 4210 Passcode: 973121",1591
