unidoc_crm_0181,4,page-2-chunk-1,2,0.5171334743499756,0.015424552373588085,"YewdaleVitesse® fitting instructions Part no: 1011 2 Fitting Instructions YewdaleVitesse® Curtain Tracks (7600W) 1. Loops in pull cords, chains, tapes and inner cords that operate the product can cause strangulation 2. To avoid strangulation and entanglement, keep cords out of the reach of young children. Cords may become wrapped around a child’s neck 3. Move beds, cots and furniture away from window covering cords 4. Do not tie cords together . Make sure cords do not twist and create a loop Safety Instructions:",517
unidoc_crm_0181,5,page-5-chunk-1,5,0.36294156312942505,0.008315778337419033,"Call: +44 (0)1268 570900 Fax: +44 (0)1268 732509 Email: enquiries@yewdale.co.uk Visit: www.yewdale.co.uk 5 1. Unpack the track and brackets 2. If the track is top fix, refer to points 3, 4, 8, 9 and 10. If face fix, refer to points 5, 6, 7 , 8, 9 and 10. 3. For top fix, insert the brackets onto the track at 800mm spacing, ensuring that there are no brackets further than 100mm in from either end. Once in place, tighten the screws to ensure the brackets are 90 degrees to the track. 4. Lift the track into its desired position and fix using the appropriate screws. 5. Fix the face fix brackets in position, ensuring the brackets are spaced no more than 800mm apart and that there is a bracket no further than 100mm in from either end. 6. Insert the nut from the bracket into the top of the track profile. 7. Lift the track up and locate the screws provided into the nut in the top channel of the track and tighten.",916
unidoc_crm_0181,6,page-6-chunk-1,6,0.51517254114151,0.0037072529084980488,"YewdaleVitesse® fitting instructions Part no: 1011 6 Fitting Instructions YewdaleVitesse® Curtain Tracks (7600W) 8. Check that the gliders move freely within the profile. 9. Once the track is installed, put the cord weight onto the cord. If the track is top fix, a fixing must be put through the fixing ring on each of the pulleys. 10. Check that the track operates smoothly and correctly before hanging curtains. NB. Large curtain tracks are heavy and it is important that the correct fixings are used. If unsure, seek expert advice. 11. Ensure the relevant child safety device is used to comply with BS EN13120:2009+A1:2014, BS EN16433:2014 and BS EN16434:2014.",663
